WEBVTT

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.000
You must really love your job.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:23.510
The entire board will cheer when we score a goal.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.750
And when we're on a losing streak, it feels like you're attending a wake.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.470
It's the only workplace where you can feel so much passion.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.770
There's no place like this anywhere else.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.200
So says the person who collapsed.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.400
Th-That...

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:51.040
No player can sprint constantly for 90 minutes.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.730
Balance is required for everything.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.920
Look who's talking.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.330
Tsubaki, will you play well in the next one too?

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.800
Hey, you!

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.840
Why are you still grinning while you're reading that thing?

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.940
You should be working!

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.550
B-But we don't have any customers right now.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.730
I'm talking about your attitude!

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.380
That's right, dad.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.950
You too, Kota?

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.990
The players are not having an easy time.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.830
Don't be fooled!

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.630
What the?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.710
Goro!

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.840
Yama from the photo lab agreed to join us!

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.970
Really?!

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:51.230
I have been interested for quite some time now...

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:53.220
Alright! Let's do it together!

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.110
Hey, you!

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.100
Dad!

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.780
I just mentioned...

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.850
Don't be overly cheerful!

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.660
First, I'll teach you our chant!

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:02.730
Chant?

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:06.220
It's a cheer to support the team. The rhythm's very important.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.180
Don't ignore us!

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.440
I can't read him.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.660
No, I mustn't think too much. If I do that, I'll be playing right into his hands.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:32.720
It's all yours, Prince. I'll admit that you're handsome if you score.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.100
Alright!

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.480
Way to go, Prince!

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.010
It's in!

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.970
Alright!

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:01.370
Nice, Gino! You're kind of handsome!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.370
Damn, this is rough.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.880
Prince is on form!

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.510
The through pass to Akasaki for the first goal, the free kick for our second one,

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:20.140
and as for the third goal, it was also his pass that led to an opponent's handball.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:27.940
Look at this, Zaki. They're all in awe of me.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:30.190
I think you're just in awe with yourself.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:39.640
If he was more serious, focused and defensive-minded,

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:43.160
he would certainly be a national player.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:52.250
Ten minutes left, huh? We need to keep attacking till the end.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.800
Kaneyan, go get Sakai.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.050
Sera, substitution.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.020
For real?

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.490
Good job, Sera.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.830
Damn, I'm so dumb!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.980
That time...

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.540
I finally got a goal-scoring opportunity...

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:55.650
If I had gotten the ball nearer to the centre, I would've had a better shot.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.250
It's okay, you did good enough, Sera.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.280
How was it good enough, Sano?

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.030
I'm a forward!

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.160
A forward needs to score!

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:09.160
I want to score...

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.170
and celebrate it in the sparkly stadium!

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.000
And then, I'll do a back flip!

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:27.210
Wait, you can do a backflip?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.020
Not right now, but I'm practicing!

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.190
Ah...I see.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:38.290
The last time I scored, we lost.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.570
That is why I wanted to score and make it count today.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:45.950
I want to go out again.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:51.950
Why can't you go back in when you've been swapped out in soccer?!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:55.330
You can swap as many times as you want in basketball and volleyball!

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.680
He's restless, eh?

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.420
Damn it!

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.970
Go, ETU!

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:08.350
Let's score a fourth one and finish the match up!

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:11.990
Continue down, Kiyokawa!

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.350
Run, run!

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:21.990
Pass it in, Kiyo!

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:28.580
Great!

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.130
Forget it!

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.420
Saku.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.140
Oh man.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:49.990
I thought I'd score a fancy one, since we're already three up...

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:54.670
That's a pity, Prince. You could've gotten a hat-trick.

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.600
Thanks, Baki.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:00.400
I guess that's it for today.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.040
Yes!

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:17.440
Alright!

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.540
Consecutive wins!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.640
Yes!

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:24.140
What do you think, Yama? ETU won!

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:25.800
Y-Yes...

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:30.370
Hooray!

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:36.330
ETU. Their first victory on home soil.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.860
Alright!

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:48.880
This makes it a win and a loss for cup matches and a win and 3 losses for the league!

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:54.450
I guess statistically we're still far behind...

00:09:56.120 --> 00:10:00.420
But we're starting to get ourselves together. This is only the beginning!

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:33.120
Argh, I ended up pulling another all-nighter.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.780
Yokohama's No.4 on defense... Here...

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:09.450
No good. I've got to clear my head!

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.420
First he's laughing, now he's crying.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.010
He must be...

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:26.480
an abusive drunkard.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:30.490
A suspicious-looking person; gotta call the police.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.110
No! I'm not suspicious!

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:41.330
I'm a player for the club! I'm just happy, since I was out for quite some time.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.710
Wait, he's...

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:54.680
Who are you?

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:06.440
This is no good.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.940
Let's put some spirit into it! Spirit!

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:12.280
Morning!

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.010
You're noisy, Sera.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.840
That's my spirit!

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:20.920
A forward has to stay positive all the time.

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.790
I mean, I finally got my chance to start!

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:36.050
Oh yeah, seems like Natsu's back.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:40.050
He will be joining in for practices from today onwards.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:46.250
A-Are you serious?

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:00.950
Weren't you sleeping like a log? How could you have met Natsu?

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:05.910
In the morning. I saw him rolling around on the grass.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:11.970
He said that he couldn't wait, so he came over as soon as the sun rose.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:16.220
That's definitely something he would do.

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:21.720
I've been guessing ever since he first called me over...

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.030
He's a weirdo, isn't he?

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:32.600
I don't think he wants to hear that from someone who's still in bed when practice has already begun.

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:35.710
Get up already!

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:36.990
Alright, alright.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:41.240
Sheesh, why do I have to babysit you everyday?!

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:50.500
That weirdo Natsuki...

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:59.190
He only played half a season due to an injury last year, but he still ended up as ETU's top scorer.

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:02.760
My daughter wanted to see me grace the pitch.

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:05.530
Apparently, I'm her hero.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.020
Natsu...

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.600
Yo, Akasaki.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.730
Nice to meet you. It's been a while.

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:18.400
That was some goal yesterday!

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:23.050
You've got good technique!

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:24.480
Right, Sera?

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.540
Cheers...

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:38.720
If it isn't Sera! How have you been?!

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.200
Have you grown a little?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:46.900
He immediately went to what I'm self-conscious about.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:48.770
He's as insensitive as ever.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.890
You're working hard, aren't you?

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:55.650
You even made it into the starting line-up! You pushed Sakai down the pecking order, right?

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:56.970
You're really something!

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:06.070
Sakai, I didn't mean it like that! I'm sorry!

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.330
Alright, I got it!

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:10.590
He is way too insensitive.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.490
Man, that loud trumpet is back.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.090
That doesn't sound credible when it's said by you, Kuro.

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:23.720
He was out for eight months. Doesn't he feel uneasy about his position at all?

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:31.560
Other than the manager and Matsu, we're all here, huh?

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.900
Right, then let me announce this again.

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:36.860
My name is Natsuki Yotaro.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:42.610
I'll be rejoining ETU with immediate effect!

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:53.290
We thought of adding more striking options last season, but we failed.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:17:01.800
I guess you know about it, but we had an ex-national player for Argentina, Fernando.

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:08.400
He couldn't settle down in Japan.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:11.810
His morale was poor and he wasn't really outstanding.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:18.440
And the reason we're on a tight budget this season is because his salary was too high.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:21.260
I know.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:24.960
That was how the season started, so the team was in bad shape.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:31.450
But we actually managed to stop the rot and get back on track.

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:43.610
Natsuki was the one who scored in games we absolutely could not lose.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:49.390
He was doing so well that he might even have been a serious contender for top scorer,

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:53.470
but he tore his knee ligament and had to withdraw from the team.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:57.410
Ever since then, the season just went downhill.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:01.480
But we somehow managed to avoid relegation with what we had left.

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:08.450
Natsuki couldn't wait and kicked balls around, which
worsened his knee and delayed his recovery by 2 months.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:09.990
Isn't that stupid?

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:18.210
He couldn't suppress his urge to play when he's with the team, so we sent him away from the club for his rehab.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:21.000
Which is why it took so long.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.010
Thanks, Macchan, for giving me a recap.

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:33.760
Hi, Manager!

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:38.610
Nice to meet you! I'll work extra hard for the team!

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:42.020
I'll make up for the trouble I caused and help the team to win!

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:44.630
Oh yeah, sure. Nice to meet you.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:51.740
Okay, players who're involved yesterday, proceed to do a warm-down. Then, we'll review yesterday's game.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:53.630
Kaneyan, take care of the reserves.

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:55.290
Let's go.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:19:00.720
H-He's so cool. Is Tatsumi always like that?

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:05.550
He's not really being cool, but that's how he always is.

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:11.670
I wonder if I'll be okay. I'm worried, Sera...

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:16.620
I've been first-choice striker for most of the games this season.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:21.310
I was worried that I'll lose my place once Natsu comes back,

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:27.940
but now that I think about it, he just came back from rehab, plus we have a new manager.

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:34.200
On the other hand, I don't know if I'm good enough,

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:36.050
but I'm the first-choice now and I've scored a goal too.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.230
I'm fine.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.300
Be more confident!

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:46.000
Sera, everyone's gone already.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:00.660
Natsuki's doing individual training?

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.600
That's normal, isn't it? It's his first day back.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:07.110
I'm glad that he's in good spirits.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.880
I'm envious of people who don't have any worries.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:15.740
I got mobbed by female fans the other day and couldn't get out.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.620
What are you bragging about?

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:22.110
I've never really seen him frowning before.

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:24.750
He's an optimist.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:30.520
So even if he's worried, others wouldn't know.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:37.260
Ever since Tatsumi became manager, he's been calling me a lot.

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:43.210
What kind of playing style the new team is using...

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:45.210
How is training like...

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:47.970
What is expected from the strikers...

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:53.030
It's the first time he's been out for eight months.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:21:01.850
He says that he will need to start back from the bottom and push his way up.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.290
His determination this season cannot be looked down upon.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:09.550
You guys have to be on your toes.

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:13.420
I won't lose!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.050
I am a striker too!

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:20.760
Well said, Sera.

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:21.810
I'm proud of you.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:25.310
Why are you mocking me?

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:34.320
Toku, I want to practice with them.

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:37.820
Nope, you'll go overboard again.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:46.700
I wanted to put up a good performance in front of him.

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:50.840
He's looking at me!

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:54.500
Toku, send me a cross.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.030
I want to get the feel of running again.

00:21:57.030 --> 00:21:57.800
Hey!

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:01.850
Give me a high one!

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:06.480
Oh well... Don't push yourself!

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:13.840
Watch this.

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:22.950
S-See that?!

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:28.390
So about the starting line-up for the next game against the Mariners...

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:29.240
He...

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:32.750
He wasn't looking!

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:34.590
Hey, Natsuki!

00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:41.270
I thought he just got back from rehab!

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:44.200
What do you think you're doing?!

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:46.120
I won't let you kick any more balls.

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:47.600
That was dangerous.

00:22:49.150 --> 00:22:53.470
I'm screwed. Can I still retain my position?!

00:24:16.410 --> 00:24:18.650
How inconsistent can he be?

00:24:18.650 --> 00:24:21.360
I guess some new pressure is needed.

00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:23.610
Another game without a goal.

00:24:23.610 --> 00:24:25.780
I'll get benched sooner or later!

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:27.620
I'm screwed!
